150
00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:09.180
'Territory'?

151
00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.080
- Oh, you mean the math territory? - Huh?

152
00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:21.450
Damn it.

153
00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:32.519
I did feel like something was a bit off at first.

154
00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:33.530
I know now.

155
00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:36.620
An honors student's glasses.

156
00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.490
There's no way they would just throw them away like this.

157
00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:42.809
F***.

158
00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:45.060
He's crazy about getting me to top up. Damn it.

159
00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:48.459
Hey, hurry up and restore the card.

160
00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.179
I can't, my mom isn't answering my calls.

161
00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:51.130
So what if she doesn't answer?

162
00:08:51.131 --> 00:08:54.710
- Keep calling until she does, idiot! - Yes.

163
00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:00.789
What's up? F***.

164
00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.240
He hit so f***ing hard.

165
00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:05.320
F***ing hell.

166
00:09:05.970 --> 00:09:07.650
How close to death is he trying to beat someone?

167
00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:12.640
(No Entry)

168
00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:16.530
What the hell, f***.

169
00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:26.220
Why isn't she answering the phone?

170
00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.360
Come on, hurry up and restore my card.

171
00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:34.180
If you don't want to see your son's corpse, hurry up and restore the card...

172
00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.560
Never mind, Mom.

173
00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.200
I think it'll be fine now.

174
00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:52.050
Are you the owner of these glasses?

175
00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:54.889
Yes, I am.

176
00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:56.030
Thank you...

177
00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.729
Why are you staring at me like that?

178
00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:05.149
Excuse me...

179
00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:06.180
Please wait a moment.

180
00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:10.299
Hello?

181
00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:13.209
Hey Yoon Jiamin, are you at Manyik High School right now?

182
00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:14.919
Yeah, where are you guys?

183
00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:16.529
Oh my god, so funny.

184
00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:18.229
Jiamin must have set a new record.

185
00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:20.139
Why weren't you answering your phone?

186
00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:23.039
I put it on silent, afraid it would interrupt my studying.

187
00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:24.139
Hey, it's not Manyik High School,

188
00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.470
It's Manil High School across the street. Manil High School!

189
00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:29.199
I see.

190
00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.149
Psycho four-eyes, if you're at Manyik High School,

191
00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.159
what was his name again? "Yoo Jun" something.

192
00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:33.999
- Min! Min! - Right, Min.

193
00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.299
Did you see a Yoo Jun-min?

194
00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:35.950
"Yoo Jun-min"?

195
00:10:35.951 --> 00:10:37.650
He's a study group member from Manyik High School.

196
00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:40.450
Are you Yoo Jun-min?

197
00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.000
I'm with him.

198
00:10:43.001 --> 00:10:44.639
Hey, there's no time to explain on the phone.

199
00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:45.799
Just get out of there quickly.

200
00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:47.189
The real monster is about to appear...

201
00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:48.120
Is it you?

202
00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:50.580
The guy who left people hanging.

203
00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:54.140
(Se-hyun)

204
00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:05.990
What, you want to officially fight?

205
00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:08.950
(Se-hyun)

206
00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:13.049
- What happened? - Did he say "left people hanging"?

207
00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:14.539
- What should we do? - Damn it, this is bad.

208
00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:15.869
That guy named Yoon Jiamin

209
00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:17.749
might really be in trouble. There's a guy named Eom Seok-dae...

210
00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:19.750
No... that's not what she meant.

211
00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:21.720
Those guys are the ones in trouble.

212
00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:52.360
If you want to play gangsters, do it yourselves.

213
00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.640
Don't mess with people who are studying.

214
00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:04.920
Wait.

215
00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:06.180
My glasses.

216
00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:07.950
Glasses...

217
00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.020
Let's actually go to the club exchange meeting now.

218
00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:20.759
Someone proposed the "two-pizza rule".

219
00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:23.589
Assuming everyone eats two slices of pizza,

220
00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:26.749
two pizzas are about enough to feed eight people.

221
00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:30.429
We first grasped each other's strengths and weaknesses.

222
00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:32.779
Then came the study group's purpose.

223
00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:35.939
We established a specific action plan first

224
00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.889
- before starting the study group activities... - "Action plan".

225
00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:38.979
Overthinking it.

226
00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:39.810
Isn't that right?

227
00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:42.810
So we each

228
00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.659
take charge of a subject we are stronger in.

229
00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.349
Complementing each other's weaknesses...

230
00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:49.089
Even though it was called a club exchange meeting,

231
00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:51.440
it was actually just an occasion for us to listen one-sidedly.

232
00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:53.669
But their passion for studying

233
00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:56.570
and their methods of running the study group based on that,

234
00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:59.510
really taught us a lot.

235
00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:05.789
I apologize for my rude remarks earlier.

236
00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:07.160
It was my prejudice.

237
00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:10.199
I misunderstood too, I'm sorry.

238
00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.790
It was my 'sense of alienation'.

239
00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:14.070
What?

240
00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:17.859
Did you mean to say 'inferiority complex'...

241
00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:18.880
Shut up.

242
00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:21.869
I get scolded for telling you too.

243
00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:23.579
Damn it, so embarrassing.

244
00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:24.629
I'm just telling you.

245
00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:25.450
Um...

246
00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:28.119
Can I talk to you for a moment?

247
00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:28.920
Sure.

248
00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:35.580
Um...

249
00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:37.420
Thank you, and also, I'm sorry.

250
00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:39.389
Sorry for what?

251
00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:40.929
Because it seemed like you didn't recognize me,

252
00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:42.550
I was planning not to say anything.

253
00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:49.050
Do you not remember me?

254
00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:57.810
I can't let you join our study group.

255
00:13:58.300 --> 00:13:59.810
You're the last place in our class.

256
00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.030
Hey, don't make eye contact with him.

257
00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:05.750
He really has no conscience, trying to freeload off of someone.

258
00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:09.520
Are you that Yoo Jun-min from back then?

259
00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:11.820
You remember.

260
00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:13.700
Of course.

261
00:14:13.701 --> 00:14:15.200
You were always in first place.

262
00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:19.419
I'm sorry for rejecting your request to join the study group back then,

263
00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:20.910
and even mocking you.

264
00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:22.750
At that time,

265
00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:25.350
I was too arrogant just because I was good at studying.

266
00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:28.210
But after coming here, I realized

267
00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:30.750
that in this world,

268
00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:34.920
there are really, really so many people who are better than me.

269
00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:39.340
I'm just a frog in a well.

270
00:14:43.350 --> 00:14:45.819
I'm not just saying this because you saved me.

271
00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:47.620
I am truly sorry about what happened back then.

272
00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:49.210
I'm fine.

273
00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:51.230
At that time,

274
00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.210
I was only angry at myself.

275
00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:56.490
I never blamed you.

276
00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:58.760
I'm glad. First place.

277
00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:05.490
On the contrary, I was very envious.

278
00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.540
But now,

279
00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:11.360
I also have friends to study with.

280
00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:25.820
That's great.

281
00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:30.149
But thinking back on it,

282
00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:31.970
how do you remember me?

283
00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:35.720
Isn't it obvious?

284
00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:37.819
At the beginning of the semester,

285
00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:40.789
you confidently stated your goal was to be first in the whole school,

286
00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.640
but you ended up in last place.

287
00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.919
But you still kept studying despite racking your brains.

288
00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.340
How could I forget?

289
00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:53.630
Keep working hard.

290
00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:56.210
Honestly, with your perseverance,

291
00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:58.160
let alone first in the school,

292
00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:01.910
I think first in the whole country isn't impossible either.

293
00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:16.510
What's going on? Is Yoon Jiamin crying?

294
00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:19.779
- I am not. - You totally are.

295
00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:20.940
Hey, he's crying.

296
00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:23.420
- Hey, why are you crying? - Yoon Jiamin.

297
00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:28.270
Let's go, let's go.

298
00:16:28.271 --> 00:16:29.749
- I'm so happy. - Yoon Jiamin.

299
00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:31.469
- So happy. - You went knowing it was 7th floor, right?

300
00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:32.350
7th floor...

301
00:16:32.351 --> 00:16:34.500
Stop muttering and come here.

302
00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:37.390
Hurry up...

303
00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:39.280
Come here quickly, Lee Ji-woo.

304
00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:44.340
Damn it.

305
00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:48.100
Dust.

306
00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:54.610
- It's not... - What the, this spider...

307
00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:58.399
Are you sure this is the place?

308
00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.410
Wow, damn it, is this a joke?

309
00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:03.120
I'll go back and ask again.

310
00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:05.509
I'm so nervous.

311
00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:06.510
- What? - What?

312
00:17:10.910 --> 00:17:13.520
If we put the desks over here, we can also hold meetings.

313
00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:17.700
Put the schedule over there.

314
00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:19.480
Awesome.

315
00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:22.579
We are looking at the same place right now, right?

316
00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:24.910
He's in another dimension right now. Another dimension.

317
00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:27.550
Excuse me.

318
00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:32.270
Wow, this is a real spider web, right?

319
00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:33.970
Why would it be fake?

320
00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:38.650
It's dirty, don't touch it.

321
00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:40.570
Scared me to death.

322
00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:44.849
How are we supposed to study here?

323
00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:47.239
Right? How is this a study group office?

324
00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:49.619
If the leader says it is, then it is.

325
00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:52.440
Then let's start cleaning up first.

326
00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:00.450
Look at this.

327
00:18:00.920 --> 00:18:02.519
This can't be pulled at all.

328
00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:05.119
- I can't believe I'm cleaning spider webs. - Hey, move aside.

329
00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:06.799
You move aside. You can clearly pass.

330
00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:08.650
- Just do your job. - Mind your own business.

331
00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:37.750
I'll do it.

332
00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:39.930
Okay.

333
00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:44.670
Thank you.

334
00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:48.860
You're welcome.

335
00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:09.790
Han-kyung.

336
00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:11.739
A talent like you.

337
00:19:11.740 --> 00:19:15.280
Do you really have to give up the recruitment exam to go there?

338
00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:24.120
I have something to do there.

339
00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:31.450
Teacher.

340
00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:39.430
(Academic Affairs Office)

341
00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:42.109
So you're saying...

342
00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:45.419
you want to convene the Disciplinary Committee to determine Pi Han-wool's punishment?

343
00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:48.849
Yes, only then can Meteor Vocational High School change.

344
00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:50.719
Please help me, Head of Academic Affairs.

345
00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:52.560
You want me to help you?

346
00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:56.030
I'm sure you know very well what that means.

347
00:19:57.510 --> 00:20:00.129
Are you capable of doing this?

348
00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:01.460
I will try.

349
00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:04.489
Just trying once isn't enough.

350
00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:06.380
I have to bet a lot of things too.

351
00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.280
What I'm asking is,

352
00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:10.849
why should I believe you

353
00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:13.010
and place my bet on your side?

354
00:20:18.220 --> 00:20:20.599
You don't have any skills.

355
00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:24.539
Where do you get the confidence to come and ask me for something like this?

356
00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:25.440
(Investigation Data for Submitting Student Pi Han-wool to the Disciplinary Committee)

357
00:20:25.441 --> 00:20:26.699
I can bring change.

358
00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:27.480
Change what?

359
00:20:27.481 --> 00:20:28.710
Change this school.

360
00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:33.929
I'm sorry, but when you reach my age,

361
00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:36.050
you will deeply realize

362
00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:39.650
that grand ambitions alone cannot change the world.

363
00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:44.580
So I don't intend to place my bet on you.

364
00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:53.130
However, I would like to test your abilities.

365
00:20:53.570 --> 00:20:54.470
What do you think?

366
00:20:57.470 --> 00:20:59.029
(Meteor Vocational High School Study Group Members)

367
00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:00.659
I'm speechless. How did he manage it again this time?

368
00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.159
- Right? - As expected of Yoon Jiamin.

369
00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:03.890
Our leader really is different.

370
00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:21.840
What the f***.
You guys decorated the smoking room f***ing nicely.

371
00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:24.479
This is the study group office.

372
00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:26.839
If you don't want your mouth smashed into the ground,
put out that cigarette.

373
00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:29.620
What... 'Study Group'?

374
00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:35.119
A bunch of trash who suck at studying

375
00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:37.490
are acting crazy in here.

376
00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:40.219
Hey, think about it yourselves.

377
00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:42.559
Even if you gather here and study your heads off,

378
00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:46.109
can you even learn as much as one normal person?

379
00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:47.929
You'll probably just get static electricity in your brains.

380
00:21:47.930 --> 00:21:48.880
Hey, you...

381
00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:50.280
Hold it in.

382
00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:53.100
If we provoke that guy, the Vice Principal won't let us off.

383
00:21:55.570 --> 00:21:56.789
So it's you.

384
00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:58.519
First place on the 1st year fighting rankings.

385
00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:00.299
I'm first place on the studying rankings.

386
00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:02.870
(Kim Ho-min: 1st Year Study Rankings 1st Place)

387
00:22:03.290 --> 00:22:04.300
Is this it?

388
00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:06.520
If you don't want it, want to punch me?

389
00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:10.599
What's there to be proud of about being good at fighting in school?

390
00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:13.200
You, a guy who sucks completely at studying.

391
00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:19.790
That guy is really...

392
00:22:21.330 --> 00:22:22.280
You know what?

393
00:22:22.281 --> 00:22:25.119
Not knowing when to give up on things that absolutely won't work

394
00:22:25.120 --> 00:22:27.880
is also because of having a bad brain.

395
00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:30.110
Hey, Kim Se-hyun.

396
00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:36.149
What are you doing here?

397
00:22:36.150 --> 00:22:39.849
Do you have time to masturbate as the ace among these idiots?

398
00:22:39.850 --> 00:22:41.719
Shouldn't you hurry up and go out to make money?

399
00:22:41.720 --> 00:22:44.300
Are you trying to be a tutor for these guys?

400
00:22:46.440 --> 00:22:49.520
Do you guys hang out with him knowing he's a beggar?

401
00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:54.709
Alright, anyway, you guys study hard too.

402
00:22:54.710 --> 00:22:56.790
We have to engage in healthy competition with each other.

403
00:22:59.430 --> 00:23:03.970
Ah, oh my, hello Teacher.

404
00:23:04.550 --> 00:23:05.950
Keep up the good work today too.

405
00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:09.110
Good luck.

406
00:23:12.100 --> 00:23:13.100
Se-hyun.

407
00:23:13.100 --> 00:23:13.960
Yeah.

408
00:23:15.220 --> 00:23:18.329
How much time do we have left until the midterm exams?

409
00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:19.090
Why?

410
00:23:19.091 --> 00:23:20.610
We have to beat him with studying.

411
00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:28.040
We need to clearly understand ourselves first, right?

412
00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:32.320
These are your placement exam scores.

413
00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:34.570
Lee Ji-woo.

414
00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:37.329
Average 14 points.

415
00:23:37.330 --> 00:23:40.660
School ranking out of 220 people:

416
00:23:41.390 --> 00:23:42.680
Rank 180.

417
00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:44.900
What?

418
00:23:44.901 --> 00:23:47.609
- Lee Joon, average 31 points. - What?

419
00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:50.269
School ranking: Rank 132.

420
00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:52.409
Damn it, I'm actually worse than Gochujang?

421
00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:53.770
I'm an intelligence-type player!

422
00:23:54.150 --> 00:23:55.299
I'm going to gouge your eyes out!

423
00:23:55.300 --> 00:23:56.609
- Choi Hee-won. - Yes.

424
00:23:56.610 --> 00:23:58.509
Average 29 points.

425
00:23:58.510 --> 00:24:01.360
School ranking: Rank 162.

426
00:24:02.010 --> 00:24:04.560
Hee-won totally looks like a top student though.

427
00:24:05.380 --> 00:24:06.370
Yoon Jiamin.

428
00:24:07.340 --> 00:24:09.220
- Yes. - Total score 25 points.

429
00:24:10.150 --> 00:24:12.940
Not average, but total score 25 points.

430
00:24:13.440 --> 00:24:15.710
Average is 8 points.

431
00:24:16.460 --> 00:24:19.350
School ranking: Rank 219.

432
00:24:21.530 --> 00:24:23.259
Psycho four-eyes got 8 points?

433
00:24:23.260 --> 00:24:25.189
Hey, you wouldn't score that low even if you guessed!

434
00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:27.210
Lastly, Kim Se-hyun.

435
00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:31.719
Average 95 points.

436
00:24:31.720 --> 00:24:34.260
School ranking: Rank 2.

437
00:24:35.120 --> 00:24:36.100
Rank 2 in the whole school?

438
00:24:36.101 --> 00:24:38.180
Are you a scammer?

439
00:24:39.080 --> 00:24:40.679
That's amazing!

440
00:24:40.680 --> 00:24:41.580
It's nothing.

441
00:24:43.060 --> 00:24:45.069
Aside from Se-hyun here,

442
00:24:45.070 --> 00:24:47.100
everyone's grades are at the bottom, right?

443
00:24:48.320 --> 00:24:50.039
But if we work hard starting now,

444
00:24:50.040 --> 00:24:52.490
our grades might miraculously improve, right Teacher?

445
00:24:53.140 --> 00:24:54.150
Jiamin.

446
00:24:55.080 --> 00:24:57.200
There are no miracles when it comes to grades.

447
00:24:59.570 --> 00:25:03.290
Of course, I mean at a normal high school.

448
00:25:03.790 --> 00:25:05.719
But this is Meteor Vocational High School.

449
00:25:05.720 --> 00:25:07.709
There are 20 days left until the midterms.

450
00:25:07.710 --> 00:25:10.689
From now on, as long as you listen carefully to what I say,

451
00:25:10.690 --> 00:25:11.830
you can do it.

452
00:25:14.430 --> 00:25:15.469
I'm so hungry.

453
00:25:15.470 --> 00:25:16.609
- Even now? - Yeah.

454
00:25:16.610 --> 00:25:18.969
Ah, actually I heard something earlier.

455
00:25:18.970 --> 00:25:19.840
What is it?

456
00:25:20.280 --> 00:25:23.249
- You said you were going to form a study group in school, right? - Yes.

457
00:25:23.250 --> 00:25:28.060
Then raise those students' school rankings by 10 places.

458
00:25:29.160 --> 00:25:32.029
What, do you think it's too difficult?

459
00:25:32.030 --> 00:25:32.990
No.

460
00:25:33.830 --> 00:25:35.289
I'll try.

461
00:25:35.290 --> 00:25:39.689
I will raise the grades of the study group students by 10 places.

462
00:25:39.690 --> 00:25:40.899
School ranking raised by 10 places?

463
00:25:40.900 --> 00:25:41.720
Yeah.

464
00:25:42.350 --> 00:25:43.230
All of us?

465
00:25:43.230 --> 00:25:44.130
Yeah.

466
00:25:44.730 --> 00:25:46.489
I'm so jealous of you, psycho four-eyes.

467
00:25:46.490 --> 00:25:48.080
It must be super easy for you.

468
00:25:49.280 --> 00:25:50.919
What about Se-hyun?

469
00:25:50.920 --> 00:25:52.269
He's second place.

470
00:25:52.270 --> 00:25:53.809
Does he have to be first in the whole school?

471
00:25:53.810 --> 00:25:54.899
- Wow. - Wow.

472
00:25:54.900 --> 00:25:56.429
That's super hard.

473
00:25:56.430 --> 00:25:58.509
Everyone, I'm going home first.

474
00:25:58.510 --> 00:26:00.139
- Oh. - Aren't you hungry?

475
00:26:00.140 --> 00:26:01.249
Have some tteokbokki before you go!

476
00:26:01.250 --> 00:26:02.979
I have plans, I have to go now.

477
00:26:02.980 --> 00:26:03.800
Bye.

478
00:26:04.640 --> 00:26:05.669
What's up with him?

479
00:26:05.670 --> 00:26:07.510
Is he scared because he heard he has to be first place?

480
00:26:08.450 --> 00:26:09.550
Want to go eat tteokbokki?

481
00:26:10.200 --> 00:26:12.109
- Let's go! - Want to go?

482
00:26:12.110 --> 00:26:13.600
- Let's go eat tteokbokki! - Want to go?

483
00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:21.279
I'm on my way.

484
00:26:21.280 --> 00:26:23.480
You punk, don't you take your father's words seriously at all?

485
00:26:23.910 --> 00:26:26.770
You have to come to the site immediately after school!

486
00:26:38.720 --> 00:26:40.600
- Kim Se-hyun. - Yes.

487
00:26:47.100 --> 00:26:47.490
- Choi Jong-hwa. - Yes.

488
00:26:47.491 --> 00:26:49.360
(English: Seho Elementary School 3rd Grade Subject Test)
- Choi Jong-hwa. - Yes.

489
00:26:52.430 --> 00:26:53.630
Kim Ho-min.

490
00:26:59.360 --> 00:27:01.679
You won't stay home properly,

491
00:27:01.680 --> 00:27:03.349
always running around everywhere getting scammed.

492
00:27:03.350 --> 00:27:05.799
Do you think I'm wasting money on purpose?

493
00:27:05.800 --> 00:27:07.819
How long do we have to live like this?

494
00:27:07.820 --> 00:27:09.719
- F***. - Are you crazy?

495
00:27:09.720 --> 00:27:13.340
- Enough! - Are you crazy, bastard?

496
00:27:14.740 --> 00:27:15.860
You two stop fighting.

497
00:27:25.430 --> 00:27:26.969
Beggar boy.

498
00:27:26.970 --> 00:27:28.929
People who don't live in our building

499
00:27:28.930 --> 00:27:30.819
aren't allowed to play at the playground.

500
00:27:30.820 --> 00:27:32.569
Why do you keep coming here?

501
00:27:32.570 --> 00:27:33.850
Are you a beggar?

502
00:27:37.370 --> 00:27:38.300
Se-hyun.

503
00:27:41.070 --> 00:27:43.010
Didn't you have plans?

504
00:27:43.440 --> 00:27:45.260
Yeah, I did.

505
00:27:47.650 --> 00:27:49.059
Want to walk together?

506
00:27:49.060 --> 00:27:50.799
We seem to be going the same way.

507
00:27:50.800 --> 00:27:51.640
Together?

508
00:27:52.760 --> 00:27:54.389
Ah, if you don't want to, then next time.

509
00:27:54.390 --> 00:27:55.710
I never said I didn't want to.

510
00:27:56.340 --> 00:27:58.810
- Okay, let's go together. - Mm.

511
00:28:05.720 --> 00:28:07.190
Thank you for that day.

512
00:28:07.640 --> 00:28:08.520
That day?

513
00:28:09.120 --> 00:28:12.330
Didn't you go with me to the police station?

514
00:28:13.100 --> 00:28:14.220
That day.

515
00:28:17.420 --> 00:28:19.320
Actually, I didn't do much that day.

516
00:28:20.470 --> 00:28:24.510
You calmly explained the situation to the police.

517
00:28:25.010 --> 00:28:27.139
If it was just me,

518
00:28:27.140 --> 00:28:28.980
I probably wouldn't have even dared to step into the police station.

519
00:28:30.340 --> 00:28:31.790
What's there to thank me for?

520
00:28:33.250 --> 00:28:35.350
The truly great one is Yoon Jiamin.

521
00:28:35.870 --> 00:28:38.599
He beat up real gangsters.

522
00:28:38.600 --> 00:28:41.590
He also single-handedly cleaned up a delinquent school
and saved Manil High School.

523
00:28:42.650 --> 00:28:45.080
In my eyes, he's like a superhero from a comic book.

524
00:28:45.910 --> 00:28:47.619
If Yoon Jiamin

525
00:28:47.620 --> 00:28:48.999
is the main character,

526
00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:50.800
then I am the one beside him,

527
00:28:51.590 --> 00:28:53.000
Friend Number 3.

528
00:28:53.950 --> 00:28:55.150
That's the kind of role I'd have, right?

529
00:28:56.410 --> 00:28:57.400
Um...

530
00:28:58.880 --> 00:29:00.319
I think...

531
00:29:00.320 --> 00:29:04.310
you underestimate yourself too much.

532
00:29:05.240 --> 00:29:07.769
That computer with the video from before,

533
00:29:07.770 --> 00:29:10.079
you were the one who destroyed it in front of the student council.

534
00:29:10.080 --> 00:29:12.680
That's not something just anyone could do.

535
00:29:13.760 --> 00:29:17.709
I also think Jiamin is really great,

536
00:29:17.710 --> 00:29:20.400
but I think you are too, Se-hyun.

537
00:29:21.300 --> 00:29:23.650
Really great.

538
00:29:25.160 --> 00:29:26.390
- Really? - Mm.

539
00:29:38.450 --> 00:29:39.230
Huh?

540
00:29:40.240 --> 00:29:41.380
It's the beggar boy.

541
00:29:55.270 --> 00:29:56.360
Come here.

542
00:30:02.120 --> 00:30:03.050
My goodness.

543
00:30:04.400 --> 00:30:05.390
You unweaned brat.

544
00:30:05.391 --> 00:30:07.279
You're actually dating now.

545
00:30:07.280 --> 00:30:09.449
What a thoroughly unfilial bastard.

546
00:30:09.450 --> 00:30:12.060
Get over here...

547
00:30:13.540 --> 00:30:15.319
It's because you live such an absurd life

548
00:30:15.320 --> 00:30:16.619
that you'll always be a loser.

549
00:30:16.620 --> 00:30:17.720
Stop hitting him.

550
00:30:18.380 --> 00:30:21.089
You dare to worry about someone else, you bitch?

551
00:30:21.090 --> 00:30:23.640
Hey, you're lucky you met me today.

552
00:30:24.600 --> 00:30:26.229
You cheap woman.

553
00:30:26.230 --> 00:30:28.909
You were so arrogant last time, let's see you be arrogant today too.

554
00:30:28.910 --> 00:30:29.590
What's wrong?

555
00:30:29.591 --> 00:30:31.770
Embarrassed in front of a boy?

556
00:30:32.140 --> 00:30:32.970
Hey.

557
00:30:33.560 --> 00:30:34.670
That's enough, you guys.

558
00:30:35.350 --> 00:30:37.159
- What do you mean 'enough'? It's nowhere near enough. - Come here.

559
00:30:37.160 --> 00:30:39.389
F***, nowhere near enough!

560
00:30:39.390 --> 00:30:41.509
You two idiots can't even take care of yourselves,

561
00:30:41.510 --> 00:30:43.989
and you're trying to act tough?

562
00:30:43.990 --> 00:30:45.849
Hey, but a girl of your level,

563
00:30:45.850 --> 00:30:47.989
why are you hanging out with a loser like this?

564
00:30:47.990 --> 00:30:50.249
This kid doesn't even have the money to treat you to gimbap.

565
00:30:50.250 --> 00:30:51.710
Look at his shabby appearance.

566
00:30:52.780 --> 00:30:54.549
And this is him supposedly dressed up!

567
00:30:54.550 --> 00:30:55.729
F***.

568
00:30:55.730 --> 00:30:57.120
Right, Se-hyun?

569
00:30:59.260 --> 00:31:00.130
F***.

570
00:31:04.490 --> 00:31:05.310
Se-hyun.

571
00:31:05.850 --> 00:31:09.589
Do you think fighting back at this moment will work?

572
00:31:09.590 --> 00:31:11.559
Do you think hanging out with Yoon Jiamin for a while

573
00:31:11.560 --> 00:31:13.469
will make you a big shot too?

574
00:31:13.470 --> 00:31:15.080
Idiot, f***ing loser.

575
00:31:17.350 --> 00:31:18.270
Kids.

576
00:31:19.720 --> 00:31:21.679
We still have to make this kid do hard labor,

577
00:31:21.680 --> 00:31:23.319
don't break his bones.

578
00:31:23.320 --> 00:31:24.799
Just beat him up a bit and let him go.

579
00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:27.860
- See you later, bye!
- Rock, paper, scissors!

580
00:31:34.420 --> 00:31:35.520
Ho-min, are you okay?

581
00:31:37.500 --> 00:31:38.640
Are you crazy?

582
00:31:39.150 --> 00:31:40.679
Do you want to fight me?

583
00:31:40.680 --> 00:31:42.179
No, I want to play a game with you.

584
00:31:42.180 --> 00:31:43.190
Forehead flicking game.

585
00:31:43.790 --> 00:31:45.979
Just ten rounds, the winner takes all.

586
00:31:45.980 --> 00:31:47.189
The loser is the loser.

587
00:31:47.190 --> 00:31:49.209
Are you in a hurry to get expelled?

588
00:31:49.210 --> 00:31:50.589
- I'm right, aren't I? - Rock, paper, scissors!

589
00:31:50.590 --> 00:31:51.390
Rock, paper, scissors!

590
00:31:54.610 --> 00:31:55.560
I won again.

591
00:32:02.170 --> 00:32:03.130
2 to 0.

592
00:32:03.131 --> 00:32:05.430
Rock, paper, scissors!

593
00:32:08.170 --> 00:32:09.410
You didn't throw anything this time.

594
00:32:10.030 --> 00:32:11.560
- Come closer. - Film it quickly...

595
00:32:22.300 --> 00:32:25.460
I have camera phobia, sorry.

596
00:32:31.590 --> 00:32:32.899
- Se-hyun. - Hey, run!

597
00:32:32.900 --> 00:32:33.970
Are you okay?

598
00:32:37.100 --> 00:32:38.050
Se-hyun.

599
00:32:50.920 --> 00:32:52.529
Sorry, it's all my fault.

600
00:32:52.530 --> 00:32:53.720
No, it's not.

601
00:32:54.470 --> 00:32:56.060
I'm fine.

602
00:33:07.680 --> 00:33:09.159
They called us losers,

603
00:33:09.160 --> 00:33:10.760
but we are the real winners, right?

604
00:33:12.820 --> 00:33:14.190
You are the winner.

605
00:33:15.600 --> 00:33:16.310
What?

606
00:33:20.400 --> 00:33:21.700
I'm leaving first.

607
00:33:34.650 --> 00:33:35.819
I'm back...

608
00:33:35.820 --> 00:33:37.499
Why aren't you out making money?

609
00:33:37.500 --> 00:33:39.520
I told you to come to the construction site to learn.

610
00:33:40.360 --> 00:33:41.640
Is that too much to ask?

611
00:33:43.130 --> 00:33:44.530
Did I say I wouldn't make money?

612
00:33:45.330 --> 00:33:47.169
I'll go make money after I graduate high school.

613
00:33:47.170 --> 00:33:48.359
What about our current debts?

614
00:33:48.360 --> 00:33:50.750
How are you going to pay off the debt your mother owes?

615
00:33:52.090 --> 00:33:53.550
I will pay it.

616
00:33:54.130 --> 00:33:56.219
Even though I didn't incur it, I will still pay it.

617
00:33:56.220 --> 00:33:58.000
Look at the way this kid talks.

618
00:33:58.440 --> 00:34:00.229
Where are you glaring when you talk to me?

619
00:34:00.230 --> 00:34:01.090
Dad.

620
00:34:01.660 --> 00:34:04.110
Right now, more than the blood on your son's face,

621
00:34:04.820 --> 00:34:07.020
you care more about losing face in front of the people at the construction site, don't you?

622
00:34:07.550 --> 00:34:10.209
Are you afraid people won't recognize that you're your mother's son?

623
00:34:10.210 --> 00:34:11.219
Look at how you speak.

624
00:34:11.220 --> 00:34:12.629
It's just a small debt,

625
00:34:12.630 --> 00:34:14.570
yet you constantly bring up my mother for everything.

626
00:34:16.790 --> 00:34:19.120
Before she became my mother, wasn't she your wife?

627
00:34:20.980 --> 00:34:21.670
Damn it.

628
00:34:21.670 --> 00:34:22.360
You...

629
00:34:24.170 --> 00:34:27.070
Fine, get out. Just like your mother...

630
00:34:40.290 --> 00:34:41.579
Why did you come back?

631
00:34:41.580 --> 00:34:42.869
Let's go to my house.

632
00:34:42.870 --> 00:34:43.640
What?

633
00:34:46.020 --> 00:34:47.000
Actually...

634
00:34:48.440 --> 00:34:50.320
I share some similarities with you.

635
00:34:51.030 --> 00:34:52.410
So let's go to my house.

636
00:34:53.300 --> 00:34:54.550
Forget it, go by yourself.

637
00:34:56.120 --> 00:34:57.219
Where are you going to sleep?

638
00:34:57.220 --> 00:34:59.330
After ten o'clock, there's nowhere that will take you in.

639
00:35:00.250 --> 00:35:02.809
If we just hurry and take a taxi now to get home before curfew,

640
00:35:02.810 --> 00:35:04.310
my mom won't say much.

641
00:35:07.730 --> 00:35:08.990
What about the taxi fare?

642
00:35:09.790 --> 00:35:11.719
It's going to cost over ten thousand won from here.

643
00:35:11.720 --> 00:35:13.260
It's fine, I'll pay.

644
00:35:23.090 --> 00:35:24.710
You probably don't understand,

645
00:35:25.510 --> 00:35:27.560
why I would do this for a mere ten thousand won.

646
00:35:29.840 --> 00:35:32.610
But friends can help each other out, right?

647
00:35:33.400 --> 00:35:34.310
Yeah.

648
00:35:34.840 --> 00:35:36.520
Friends can definitely help each other out.

649
00:35:39.540 --> 00:35:41.420
I'm also very thankful for your help.

650
00:35:42.280 --> 00:35:44.060
But why is it always you helping me?

651
00:35:44.820 --> 00:35:46.100
Is it because I'm always inferior?

652
00:35:48.720 --> 00:35:50.390
That's right, I've never won.

653
00:35:51.150 --> 00:35:52.269
Whether at school or at home.

654
00:35:52.270 --> 00:35:53.170
Se-hyun.

655
00:35:57.490 --> 00:36:00.930
Just pretend I'm being unreasonable.

656
00:36:01.650 --> 00:36:03.340
It's getting late, you should hurry home.

657
00:36:21.290 --> 00:36:23.160
(Mom)
It's 10 o'clock in 25 minutes.

658
00:36:48.540 --> 00:36:49.870
Damn it.

659
00:36:53.710 --> 00:36:54.979
They called us losers,

660
00:36:54.980 --> 00:36:56.500
but we are the real winners, right?

661
00:36:58.040 --> 00:36:59.400
You are the winner.

662
00:37:00.530 --> 00:37:01.780
Is it because I'm always inferior?

663
00:37:02.220 --> 00:37:03.850
That's right, I've never won.

664
00:37:04.610 --> 00:37:05.970
Whether at school or at home.

665
00:37:12.750 --> 00:37:14.420
(Sewoon Middle School 2nd Year, 2nd Semester History Midterm Exam)

666
00:37:17.600 --> 00:37:18.810
Sigh...

667
00:37:28.900 --> 00:37:30.870
(6.2km 09:59 PM)

668
00:37:44.540 --> 00:37:45.630
You punk.

669
00:37:47.480 --> 00:37:50.330
You really are unlucky.

670
00:37:51.490 --> 00:37:53.440
Hey, I'm...

671
00:37:59.580 --> 00:38:01.849
in an extremely bad mood.

672
00:38:01.850 --> 00:38:04.909
So I really don't want to just go home.

673
00:38:04.910 --> 00:38:07.949
I have to punch you a few more times to be able to sleep tonight.

674
00:38:07.950 --> 00:38:09.110
So just let me hit you.

675
00:38:22.520 --> 00:38:23.640
F*** off.

676
00:38:24.610 --> 00:38:25.830
I've been...

677
00:38:26.560 --> 00:38:29.240
beaten up all day today, you little brat.

678
00:38:30.010 --> 00:38:31.610
Are you crazy, kid?

679
00:38:32.090 --> 00:38:35.150
Then spend the rest of the day getting beaten up too, you punk.

680
00:38:39.070 --> 00:38:39.970
It's probably your dad.

681
00:38:39.971 --> 00:38:41.269
You should answer it...

682
00:38:41.270 --> 00:38:42.270
Answer it.

683
00:38:42.271 --> 00:38:44.550
You need to tell him you're busy getting beaten up today and will be home late.

684
00:38:45.990 --> 00:38:46.810
5

685
00:38:47.490 --> 00:38:48.450
4

686
00:38:48.451 --> 00:38:49.590
3, 2, 1

687
00:38:52.970 --> 00:38:53.930
Oh my.

688
00:39:00.600 --> 00:39:01.670
Look at this guy.

689
00:39:02.150 --> 00:39:03.020
What's your deal?

690
00:39:05.200 --> 00:39:06.490
Damn it.

691
00:39:18.390 --> 00:39:20.100
F***.

692
00:39:21.340 --> 00:39:22.379
You're doing great.

693
00:39:22.380 --> 00:39:25.289
Put your phone in your pocket and take a boxing stance.

694
00:39:25.290 --> 00:39:26.879
Are you watching me right now?

695
00:39:26.880 --> 00:39:27.790
Didn't you go home?

696
00:39:27.790 --> 00:39:28.500
Yeah.

697
00:39:28.501 --> 00:39:30.029
I'm watching, so don't worry.

698
00:39:30.030 --> 00:39:33.389
Clench your right fist, imagine there's a wall on your left.

699
00:39:33.390 --> 00:39:34.850
And smash into that wall.

700
00:39:35.280 --> 00:39:36.030
What are you talking about?

701
00:39:36.031 --> 00:39:37.179
What wall am I supposed to smash?

702
00:39:37.180 --> 00:39:38.909
What the hell is this crazy guy saying?

703
00:39:38.910 --> 00:39:40.589
Has he completely lost his mind?

704
00:39:40.590 --> 00:39:41.730
Don't you want to win?

705
00:39:43.080 --> 00:39:43.830
Now!

706
00:39:46.060 --> 00:39:48.100
- You dare block it? F***! - Do it again, the same way!

707
00:39:51.380 --> 00:39:52.340
Turn left.

708
00:39:52.720 --> 00:39:53.870
Sit down towards the right.

709
00:39:59.350 --> 00:40:00.509
You're doing great.

710
00:40:00.510 --> 00:40:01.860
Keep doing exactly this, while dodging...

711
00:40:04.150 --> 00:40:05.000
Hey.

712
00:40:05.390 --> 00:40:06.479
Hey, Yoon Jiamin.

713
00:40:06.480 --> 00:40:08.009
Hey.

714
00:40:08.010 --> 00:40:10.619
You're dead today, punk.

715
00:40:10.620 --> 00:40:12.310
Punk.

716
00:40:13.450 --> 00:40:14.480
Roll backward! Backward!

717
00:40:15.040 --> 00:40:15.750
No...

718
00:40:17.390 --> 00:40:19.640
Then cover your face, roll to the right, and get up!

719
00:40:20.880 --> 00:40:22.570
Hey!

720
00:40:40.400 --> 00:40:42.480
Even if it's not a grand victory, it's okay.

721
00:41:00.290 --> 00:41:02.040
What can comfort the feeling of failure

722
00:41:05.470 --> 00:41:07.230
isn't a test paper with 100 points,

723
00:41:42.080 --> 00:41:44.070
but a single circle is enough.

724
00:41:54.560 --> 00:41:58.600
"Study Group"

725
